# Capa 0 refactor (DEPLOY_VPS_PLAN.md): web ya NO ejecuta migrate/collectstatic/
# seed_permissions inline. Esos pasos son `release` — one-shot antes de que
# arranquen los workers. Razón: con múltiples workers/instances, encadenar
# migraciones en cada boot es race condition (varios `migrate` simultáneos
# contra la misma DB) y degrada el time-to-ready.
#
# Plataformas:
#   - Docker Compose (VPS):  servicio `release` con condition: service_completed_successfully
#                            corre `/app/scripts/release.sh` antes de levantar `backend`.
#   - Railway / Heroku:      el comando `release` se ejecuta una vez por deploy
#                            (lifecycle nativo). El comando `web` solo arranca gunicorn.
release: ./scripts/release.sh
web: gunicorn config.wsgi:application --bind 0.0.0.0:$PORT --workers ${GUNICORN_WORKERS:-3} --threads ${GUNICORN_THREADS:-2} --timeout ${GUNICORN_TIMEOUT:-60} --max-requests 1000 --max-requests-jitter 100 --access-logfile - --error-logfile - --log-level info

# Analytics nightly snapshot. Idempotent + per-org advisory locked, so safe
# even if double-fired. Per-org failures isolated; non-zero exit
# code on any org failure (wire alerting on this).
# Docker Compose (VPS): host crontab → `docker compose exec -T backend python manage.py build_daily_metrics`
# Recommended: 06:00 UTC daily (covers Mexico GMT-6/-7/-8 yesterday end-of-day).
nightly_snapshots: python manage.py build_daily_metrics
# Anchor invariant audit. Runs after the snapshot job so any lurking
# anchor corruption surfaces. Exit 1 = unresolved provenance, exit 2 =
# invariant violation (P1).
nightly_anchor_audit: python manage.py audit_anchor_integrity --json
# JWT blacklist + outstanding token cleanup. ADR p20 — sin esto las
# tablas crecen lineales con cada login/refresh/change-password.
nightly_flush_jwt: python manage.py flushexpiredtokens
